{"Title":"An Act relative to stroke system of care","BillNumber":"H3618","DocketNumber":"HD1561","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MJC1","Name":"Mark J. Cusack","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MJC1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T15:08:19.913"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MJC1","Name":"Mark J. Cusack","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MJC1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T15:08:19.9133333"},{"Id":"SSH1","Name":"Steven S. Howitt","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SSH1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-31T10:58:11.2233333"},{"Id":"JAG1","Name":"Jessica Ann Giannino","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-31T12:29:09.64"},{"Id":"JPL1","Name":"Jack Patrick Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JPL1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-01T13:52:53.3666667"},{"Id":"AJP1","Name":"Angelo J. Puppolo, Jr.","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AJP1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-01T13:52:53.3666667"},{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-02T14:57:31.0133333"},{"Id":"AFC1","Name":"Antonio F. D. Cabral","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AFC1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-02T14:57:31.0133333"},{"Id":"CAD1","Name":"Carol A. Doherty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CAD1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-02T16:40:27.7833333"},{"Id":"jwm1","Name":"Joseph W. McGonagle, Jr.","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jwm1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T13:37:20.6633333"},{"Id":"ERP1","Name":"Edward R. Philips","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/ERP1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-14T12:51:10.6433333"},{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-14T13:30:43.1433333"},{"Id":"DCG1","Name":"Denise C. Garlick","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DCG1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-15T13:33:38.0833333"},{"Id":"KLG1","Name":"Kate Lipper-Garabedian","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/KLG1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-23T10:41:53.25"},{"Id":"HEK1","Name":"Hannah Kane","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/HEK1","ResponseDate":"2023-03-01T16:41:35.5966667"},{"Id":"T_V1","Name":"Tommy Vitolo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_V1","ResponseDate":"2023-03-20T16:09:59.3633333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3618/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Cusack of Braintree, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3618) of Mark J. Cusack and others relative to establishing a statewide standard prehospital care protocol related to the assessment, treatment and transport of stroke patients.  Public Health.","DocumentText":"\tNotwithstanding any general or special law to the contrary, not later than 180 days after the effective date of this act, the department of public health shall promulgate regulations that create: (i) a statewide standard prehospital care protocol related to the assessment, treatment and transport of stroke patients by emergency medical services providers to a hospital designated by the department to care for stroke patients; provided, however, that the protocol shall be based on national evidence-based guidelines for transport of stroke patients, consider transport that crosses state lines and include plans for the triage and transport of suspected stroke patients including, but not limited to, those who may have an emergent large vessel occlusion, to an appropriate facility within a specified timeframe following the onset of symptoms and additional criteria to determine which level of care is the most appropriate destination; provided further, that the department shall develop said protocol in consultation with the expert stroke advisory taskforce established pursuant to subsection (c) of section 51L of chapter 111 of the General Laws; and (ii) recommended national evidence-based quality and utilization measure sets for stroke care for use by the center for health information and analysis pursuant to section 14 of chapter 12C of the General Laws; provided, however, that the department shall consider measures in current use in national quality improvement programs including, but not limited to, the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services, the National Quality Forum, the Paul Coverdell National Acute Stroke Program or other nationally-recognized data platforms.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J16","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J16"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}